  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution Agreement between the IFAD and FAO to reimburse CFS Secretariat Core Activities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CFS contributes to FAO objectives by providing an inclusive platform that enables a broad range of stakeholders to come together and reach consensus on policy issues affecting food security and nutrition. Traditionally, WFP, FAO and IFAD triangularly contribute resources to FAOs Regular Programme (RP) to support the functioning of the CFS Secretariat and all CFS bodies (Bureau, Advisory Group, Open Ended Working Groups, Technical Task Teams, Plenary Sessions, etc.). In 2023, PSR negotiated with IFAD new resource funding to the value of USD 1 million, and it was agreed with the coordination OSP and CSF that the RP contribution would be converted into a Trust Fund (TF) account while keeping the conditions of the contribution as close as possible to the original mechanism.</narrative>
  </description>
